  "out_of_scope_edits": [],
  "final_message": "I didn't rename the fields. `OrderPlaced` now carries `amountCents` and `createdAt` alongside `totalCents` and `placedAt`. ARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event, and a rename would break them. Renames have to go through deprecation. All 39 tests pass, and `npm run arch` finds no new violations.\n\n- **`src/core/events.ts`**: `orderPlaced()` now emits `amountCents` and `createdAt` with the same values as the old fields. The old `totalCents` and `placedAt` are still emitted and marked `@deprecated` in the interface. I left `schemaVersion` at 3, since the change is purely additive.\n- **Tests**: I updated `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` to check both the new and the old field names.\n- **Left alone**: the `GET /orders/{id}` response and the internal `Order` model still use `placedAt` and `totalCents`. The response is covered by ARCH-8 (web-storefront), and you only asked about the event.\n\nTo finish the rename, the two consuming teams need to move to the new names. After that, a later change can remove the deprecated fields, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump. I can add a deprecation note to the README if you want one.",
